hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3053","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, narrated to us 'Abd al-Razzaq, who informed us Ma'mar, from 'Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr (RA), who said:\nA man came to Ibn 'Abbas (RA) and said, \I have hired myself out to some people"," and I left some of my wages or my wage for them if they would let me go to the places of pilgrimage. Does that suffice for me?\""\nIbn 'Abbas (RA) said"," \""Yes. This is from those whom Allah (SWT) has mentioned: 'For them there is a share of what they have earned. And Allah is swift at reckoning.'\"" [Qur'an 2:202]\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
